cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DeepCatch in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "DeepCatch v2.2.0: An Open-Source Benchmark for Panel-Based Ultra-Sensitive Detection of Circulating Tumor DNA from Real Tumor Mutations"
authors:
  - given-names: "Yu Ching"
    family-names: "Lam"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher (no institutional affiliation; verified email domain umich.edu)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9113-769X"
year: 2026
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.to-be-assigned-on-first-release"
url: "https://github.com/rollroyces/deepcatch"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rollroyces/deepcatch"
repository-companion: "https://github.com/rollroyces/cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline"
license: MIT
version: "2.2.0"
date-released: 2026-08-21
keywords:
  - "cfDNA"
  - "ctDNA"
  - "liquid biopsy"
  - "molecular residual disease (MRD)"
  - "panel LLR"
  - "fragmentomics"
  - "tumor-naive detection"
  - "open science"
  - "benchmark"
abstract: >
  DeepCatch v2.2.0 is an open-source panel-based ultra-sensitive ctDNA
  detection pipeline benchmarked against real TCGA tumor mutations. Using
  20 TCGA-LUAD patients (5,738 somatic mutations, GDC open access) as
  ground truth and a context-aware sequencing error model, we simulate
  plasma cfDNA at tumor fractions 10% down to 0.1%. At 0.1% ctDNA, panel
  log-likelihood-ratio (LLR) aggregation achieves AUC 0.921 (Sens@95%
  0.770), with paired cancer-vs-control win rate 1.000 across seeds. The
  companion cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline contributes a tumor-naive
  detection channel (cross-study pan-cancer AUC 0.9745 +/- 0.002 on 627
  FinaleDB samples from Jiang 2015 + Cristiano 2019). Naive averaging
  of the two channels achieves AUC 0.9886 (Sens@95% 0.927) — paired
  t-test: fusion > tumor-naive alone at p < 0.0001.
